.It Bq Er EEXIST
.Dv KVM_CREATE_VCPU
of an id the VM has;
.Dv KVM_CAP_SPLIT_IRQCHIP
a second time or once the VM has a vCPU;
.Dv KVM_CREATE_IRQCHIP
once a controller exists;
.Dv KVM_CREATE_PIT
or
.Dv KVM_CREATE_PIT2
once the PIT exists;
.Dv KVM_INTERRUPT
with the split controller while a vector waits;
a memory slot at guest addresses another has;
an ioeventfd that some write would match along with another;
