.Sh BUGS
At most 1024 vCPUs in a VM, with ids below 4096, and 256 memory slots.
No dirty ring, no SMM and no nested virtualization, so
no enlightened VMCS and no direct TLB flush of Hyper-V's.
Most statistics of
.Dv KVM_GET_STATS_FD
read 0.
The TSC's rate is scaled only where the processor scales it.
Of KVM's paravirtual features there are no asynchronous page faults,
paravirtual EOI or TLB flush, and without a measured TSC rate no kvmclock.
The APIC and PIT timers are checked at each entry, and the host's tick of 1 ms
makes the guest exit, so an expiry reaches the guest within a tick.
